# Ship LF everywhere, regardless of the user's git core.autocrlf.
# A stray CR at the end of a SKILL.md / command frontmatter line corrupts the
# Claude Code command/skill picker on Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true):
# the \r returns the cursor to column 0 and the picker overpaints instead of
# clearing, so scrolled-past rows stay on screen.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.woff2 binary
